+### Scale-Adaptive Gaussian Fitting for Dynamic 3DGS
+Applying the scale-adaptive Gaussian fitting method as a plug-in to dynamic 3DGS models to solve zoom-out dilation without disturbing the deformation network [S7]. Scaffold-GS and Pixel-GS lack multi-scale deformation, compromising robustness for unseen settings [S7].
+
+### E-D3DGS
+Embeds between Gaussian band and MLP for deformation prediction. Assigns each Gaussian a latent learnable embedding for unique characteristics and uses typical temporal embeddings for different frames. MLP takes latent and temporal embeddings to predict changes in position, scale, and rotation [S3, unofficial]. Separately conducts deformation for coarse and fine motions: leverages a 1D feature grid for N frames and interpolates temporally to decode embedding for fine deformation; downsamples feature grid for coarse deformation [S3, unofficial]. Uses Local Smoothness Regularization to encourage nearby Gaussians to conduct similar deformation to capture textures and fine details [S3, unofficial].
+
+### SP-GS
+Groups 3D Gaussians into superpoints using a Property Reconstruction Loss. The deformation network takes canonical position of superpoints and time as input to predict deformation, applied to Gaussians within superpoints [S3, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Depends on the deformation network size and number of Gaussians. Real-time rendering is feasible if the deformation network is lightweight [S3, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Stores canonical Gaussians plus deformation network weights. More compact than storing full 4D Gaussians for every frame [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Handles dynamic scenes (people moving, fluids) [S1, unofficial]. Can achieve real-time rendering [S3, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Performance depends on the deformation network's capacity. May struggle with complex, non-rigid deformations if the network is too simple [S3, unofficial].
